(7437890, 1175625, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I find the colours a little washy here, and the snow a little bleached out. Some more contrast would have helped give depth to the shot. I think a closer crop so that you were eliminating the ''ing'' in the No Trespassing sign would have helped the composition a bit esp as the hole is very centred here. After all, comments indicate that people can''t see the ''Private Property'' part of the sign, so you can''t assume that people *know* what the rest of the sign says.  <br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! I find the colours a little washy here, and the snow a little bleached out. Some more contrast would have helped give depth to the shot. I think a closer crop so that you were eliminating the ''ing'' in the No Trespassing sign would have helped the composition a bit esp as the hole is very centred here. After all, comments indicate that people can''t see the ''Private Property'' part of the sign, so you can''t assume that people *know* what the rest of the sign says.   Hope this helps Susan', '2016-02-17 19:45:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(7437891, 1175529, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hmmm close but no cigar this time, I''m afraid.  I like the dynamic angled comp, good focus,and punchy colours but feel that, simply put...there are just too many signs, in several different colours, all saying different things, so I think this may have led to some confusion on the voters'' part, and that means lower votes as this site tends to be very literal.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hmmm close but no cigar this time, I''m afraid.  I like the dynamic angled comp, good focus,and punchy colours but feel that, simply put...there are just too many signs, in several different colours, all saying different things, so I think this may have led to some confusion on the voters'' part, and that means lower votes as this site tends to be very literal. Hope this helps Susan', '2016-02-17 19:49:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7437892, 1175691, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Hmmm this image is a very good try at the challenge, it is a truncated sign, and I don''t mind the angle as I feel it adds interest.  I think the main problem is twofold: a lack of colour, this could have used a hit of saturation to make the image pop a little more. Second, lack of a dominant element here; no one aspect stands head and shoulders above the rest demanding your attention. The winged foot is also somewhat centred, maybe a closer crop in to it would have helped draw more attention to it. <br/> <br/>Hope this helps!  Feel free to PM me with any questions.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Hmmm this image is a very good try at the challenge, it is a truncated sign, and I don''t mind the angle as I feel it adds interest.  I think the main problem is twofold: a lack of colour, this could have used a hit of saturation to make the image pop a little more. Second, lack of a dominant element here; no one aspect stands head and shoulders above the rest demanding your attention. The winged foot is also somewhat centred, maybe a closer crop in to it would have helped draw more attention to it.  Hope this helps!  Feel free to PM me with any questions. Susan', '2016-02-17 20:01:22.000000', NULL, 0),
