(7438407, 1175717, 112828, '<td valign="top">Couldn''t miss this.  Knew the building from the thumbnail on the homepage.<br/> <br/>Congrats, great image!</td>', 'Couldn''t miss this.  Knew the building from the thumbnail on the homepage. Congrats, great image!', '2016-02-20 02:12:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7438508, 1175722, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Long exposure is a personal favourite of mine, though I don''t use it often.  And I am a huge fan of photogs who put thought and planning into their shot, so you''ve already scored twice with me in a big way :-)<br/> <br/>Now, I would not have thought this an easy challenge at all, which is partly why I sat it out!  Looking at the images that did well here, you can see that they tended to take very recognizable signs and just cut out half of the word. Some left a certain amount of guessing; others, like those featuring a stop sign whose shape and colour are recognizable the world over, had to say very little to convey their message.<br/> <br/>I feel that the main problem here is that the sign is too dominant an image, and as you want us to try and guess what the speed limit is, it might have been better to crop off the left side of the sign so it would read ''EED MIT 0'' underneath it.  Try it and see if it works for you.<br/> <br/>Please keep shooting and entering, and feel free to PM me with any questions<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Long exposure is a personal favourite of mine, though I don''t use it often.  And I am a huge fan of photogs who put thought and planning into their shot, so you''ve already scored twice with me in a big way :-) Now, I would not have thought this an easy challenge at all, which is partly why I sat it out!  Looking at the images that did well here, you can see that they tended to take very recognizable signs and just cut out half of the word. Some left a certain amount of guessing; others, like those featuring a stop sign whose shape and colour are recognizable the world over, had to say very little to convey their message. I feel that the main problem here is that the sign is too dominant an image, and as you want us to try and guess what the speed limit is, it might have been better to crop off the left side of the sign so it would read ''EED MIT 0'' underneath it.  Try it and see if it works for you. Please keep shooting and entering, and feel free to PM me with any questions Susan', '2016-02-20 21:03:12.000000', NULL, 0),
